 doing  this on your main file if done  improperly without planning beforehand  it can lead to multiple unsellable armor  unusable korok seats and or shrine orbs  a bunch of duplicated unusable arrows  you can't refill which all technically  can be fixed but it takes a lot of extra  work therefore i recommend never manual  saving until absolutely necessary double  checking your glitched outcomes through  auto saves instead or i personally still  recommend starting a fresh file or  profile as a side project third this is  much more complex than how i'm going to  explain it ist includes working with  game data save data m count offsets  desync corruption and more but for  simplicity's sake i'm going to try to  reduce the fancy words as much as  possible to focus on the visual basic  concept without further ado let's  explain the basics of breaking your file  for the easy version you need five to  six multi-shot bows at least one shock  arrow materials with at least two of  each and a shopkeeper this can be done  with beetles as stables if you'd like  but personally i like doing this in busy  towns hoteno village is a popular pick  due to being close to home to rack up  your equipment cooking pots nearby and a  good shopkeeper next thing you'll want  to do is think about what you want to  duplicate let's say for now we want to  duplicate fairies and diamonds this  process is always going to vary in  difficulty depending on what you want  but the general rule is whatever the  thing it is you want have it as close to  the right of the menu as possible you  can achieve this by selling off dropping  and picking up or eating as much as you  can before these items  now that you've got your gear and your  targets to duplicate you can start the  offsetting process let's start by  performing a basic menu overload stand  near your vendor then pull out any  multi-shot bow with the shock arrow  equipped go into the menu and then drop  the bow  then go over to the next bow and equip  the next one exit the menu then pause  again repeat this until link starts  losing some limbs and body parts  if you're still having trouble getting  him to overload fully try equipping one  elemental rod on his back to push it  just a tad more  in the meantime keep that bow equipped  and held in his hands for now now go to  the materials tab and hold four  different items in your hands  exit the menu and if link puts his arms  down you smuggled successfully if he  held these items in his hands try this  process again you don't want to see the  items in your hands now hold zr then  d-pad right and unequip the bow if done  correctly you'll now be smuggling four  items and not be overloaded anymore head  over to the shopkeeper and go ahead and  sell the entire stack of four items in  your hands  [Music]  stop talking to the shopkeeper go into  your menu and just press a on any fifth  material in your menu then exit out and  press a again to drop it  this is where the magic happens what  just happened was link tossed on the  ground one real material and four  invisible materials that never existed  because they were sold out of your hands  before you threw them this tells the  game that you deleted 4 slots but  without dropping any materials which is  called offset slots here we made four  now reload your file  the fairies and diamonds are now  duplicated  this is where i'll have to explain  what's going on behind the scenes a  little further okay let's step back and  do a simpler example of this with all  the equipment in a straight line let's  say link this time now holds a  traveler's sword a bow normal arrows  traveler's shield  five materials hearty simmered fruit  meal and his handy shiga slate and  paraglider 12 items total in normal  gameplay when you sell the four items  entirely it reduces your four slots  along with it so now you have 8 items  and everything is fine every time you  reload the game what actually happens is  the game confirms that you do indeed  have 8 items on you then delete every  single item you own starting from the  left side the weapons tab this is  because it's designed around a system  called an intrusive linked list without  pretending to know too much about this  this is a data system that remembers  things in chain order rather than  erasing and copying data individually  when you load back in the game says you  have eight items to load back in this is  called m count the game copies those  eight items into those eight slots in  that order with this system and  everything is good and dandy  now let's see what we did to mess with  this system this time same inventory but  we perform the glitch sell our items  which reduces our m count by four but  then as we exit the shopkeeper we throw  those four items on the ground which  reduces your m count by an additional  four slots but without dropping any  materials now the game thinks you have  four items in your inventory but you  actually have eight  now when reloading your save this time  you're telling the game i have four m  count the game like usual starts to  delete one by one starting from the left  once it gets to fairies though something  happens it stops counting these last  four slots are then simply carried over  when reloading because they technically  never left  that's why the originals show up at the  beginning of the materials tab because  when you reloaded it deleted those  materials starting from the left side  then got those materials and then sorted  those materials into the tabs of the  file you just loaded  so why aren't some things duplicated  like the sheikah slate and the  paraglider well there's a special check  in the game for several items saying  that you can only have one of them ever  which goes for most key items so it  won't duplicate which is great news for  us actually  there's a bunch of special exceptions  for this but the main rule is arrows and  duplicatable key items are the enemy  they fill up your inventory with  unusable stuff so try to have a file  with minimal to no arrows and less  duplicatable key items to have a better  time as complicated as just this is this  is just the base technique of inventory  slot transfer and this basic concept can  be used in complex ways to go even  farther you can reload again and again  to duplicate multiple items multiple  times bring the bow of light into any  file you want transfer basically  whatever item you want from any file  onto any save even between normal and  master mode files even start a new game  with the glitched food menu to further  glitch the save prompt into a cut scene  and load into unattended areas like the  end of the game and explore hyrule with  calamine again and defeat it and  everyone's favorite discovery so far to  unlock powerful forgotten modifiers  nintendo never released  by creating offset slots to match your  key items and 60 recipes the 60th  recipe's values corrupts the closest  equipment's modifiers and creates some  of the most powerful equipment ever seen  in the game all possible on any nintendo  switch around the world it's a broken  record now but breath of the wild's  discoveries just don't stop it's  guaranteed something will be found year  over year and the whole community puts  in a ton of work to make this research  happen  thanks for watching and if you want a  tutorial for weapon modifier corruption  let us know in the comments below for  everything else gaming keep it here on  gamespot  [Music]  [Music]
 

